Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi,

thanks for your email.

First, if there is something we could do to make 'plot(result)' play
well in 'knitr', we'll do that...

My own take to this problem when using sweave, is to use

<<results=tex,echo=FALSE>>=
figs = plot(result, single=TRUE, postscript=TRUE,
prefix="Sweave/ex1/figure-")
cat("\\begin{figure}[tbp]\n")
cat("\n")
cat("\\centering\n")
for(i in 1:length(figs)) {
    cat("\\includegraphics[width=7cm,height=7cm,angle=-90]{",
gsub("[.]eps$","",figs[i]), "}\n", sep="")
}
cat("\\caption{XXX}\n")
cat("\\label{fig:11}\n")
cat("\\end{figure}\n")
@
%

I'm not sure how to proceed otherwise. If someone has a good fix for
this, please let us know ;-)

H

