Even disregarding the std.dev./quantile confusion, it is still not
clear what you want to do.

For example, when you write "within 1 sd, 2 sd, 3 sd", _what_ is
supposed to be within
those distances of _what_, precisely?
The posterior mean is always within "a*sd" distance of itself for any
non-negative "a",
so that is clearly not what you mean.

Do you mean the distance to some pre-defined reference level?

Finn

